  "findings": [
    "REJECTED: deployment_comment_name at deployment.rs:791 tests label_to_id(label)==id to infer an unaliased identity. Explicit aliases Copper_Bay and Metal_Case collide with that transformation: fresh deploy_alias_collision and group_identity_collision emit Copper Bay/Metal Case where pinned EntityImageDescription/Cluster use Copper_Bay/Metal_Case. The link comments newly lose previously correct underscore identities. This is identity inference, not a lossless model projection. T14.23 explicitly records the missing alias/derived-id data but does not make these outputs correct.",
    "Class aliases and bare quoted names improve: class_alias_bidirectional and class_quoted_spaces match both whole-output comparator and exact producer lists. Root package recovery is bounded; default nested namespaces still emit Observatory.Dome/Upper.Middle instead of Dome/Middle, and custom separator emits West..Bay instead of Bay. These three sources PASS the shipped strict comparator because it ignores comments. T14.23 residue is explicit, but acceptance remains rejected.",
    "Nested state history projection is ineffective in emit_autonomous_scope_links: transition endpoints are first shortened through autonomous_endpoint_svg_name at state.rs:4141\u20134142, losing the [H]/[H*] prefix on nested IDs, then state_comment_endpoint is called at :4154\u20134155/:4165\u20134166. Fresh state_history_nested_identity emits Lower instead of *historical*Lower / *deephistory*Lower. Pinned StateDiagram.getHistorical/getDeepHistory constructs the synthetic name from the local group name.",
    "Reverse deployment/group links and mixed description-family ordering remain wrong on deploy_alias_collision, deploy_nested_groups, and description_kinds. These are retained whole-output failures, not newly lost comparator passes.",
    "Object-kind comment omission is supported by GeneralImageBuilder.java:180\u2013181 selecting EntityImageObject, whose drawU has no UComment. Fresh class_object_mixed has the exact Java comment list and omits only the Object comment; its whole output still fails geometry. Golden combo_class_vs_object also has the exact Java list after removal. Quoted object admission remains T14.17 and emits an empty model; it is not repaired by comment selection."
  ],
